#X text 50 88 [guicanvas] is a canvas you draw on with messages. Drawing commands are not drawn right away: they pile up in a list and are only rendered when the object gets a 'bang' (or 'end'). The list is kept afterwards \, so a redraw is usually 'clear' \, then the commands \, then 'bang'., f 66;
#X text 48 150 Coordinates are in pixels from the top left corner and colors are in RGB. The 'color' message stays in effect for every command that follows it., f 48;
#X obj 376 203 else/guicanvas 150 120;
#X obj 50 202 loadbang;
#X msg 50 228 clear \, color 60 130 210 \, ellipse 15 15 55 55 fill \, color 220 100 60 \, linewidth 3 \, rectangle 70 40 55 55 stroke \, bang, f 36;
#N canvas 169 133 1438 875 shapes 0;
#X text 30 20 Every shape takes its position and size in pixels. The rectangle \, rounded rectangle \, ellipse and path commands take a final 'fill' or 'stroke' symbol \; rectangles and ellipses default to 'fill' and paths default to 'stroke'., f 66;
#X text 30 80 The 'linewidth' message sets the width used by the stroke commands that come after it. It is not part of the drawing list \, it is applied as each command is added., f 66;
#X obj 405 256 else/guicanvas 200 200;
#X msg 30 150 clear \, color 60 130 210 \, rectangle 20 20 80 50 \, bang, f 44;
#X msg 30 180 clear \, color 60 130 210 \, linewidth 4 \, rectangle 20 20 80 50 stroke \, bang, f 44;
#X msg 30 210 clear \, color 200 80 60 \, roundedrect 20 20 100 60 12 \, bang, f 44;
#X msg 30 240 clear \, color 60 160 90 \, ellipse 30 30 90 90 \, bang, f 44;
#X msg 30 270 clear \, color 40 40 40 \, linewidth 2 \, line 10 10 180 180 \, bang, f 44;
#X msg 30 300 clear \, color 150 60 190 \, path 20 150 60 40 100 150 140 40 180 150 stroke \, bang, f 44;
#X msg 30 330 clear \, color 150 60 190 \, path 20 150 100 40 180 150 fill \, bang, f 44;
#X msg 30 360 clear \, color 20 20 20 \, linewidth 3 \, curve 20 180 40 20 160 20 180 180 \, bang, f 44;
#X msg 30 390 clear \, color 235 235 245 \, fillall \, color 200 60 60 \, ellipse 60 60 80 80 \, bang, f 44;
#X text 30 430 'fillall' paints the whole canvas with the current color \, which is handy as the first command of a redraw., f 44;
#X text 30 470 'arc' takes the same x/y/width/height box as 'ellipse' plus a start and end angle in degrees \, measured from the top and going clockwise. 'stroke' draws the arc itself and 'fill' fills the pie slice back to the centre., f 66;
#X text 30 530 'quad' is a quadratic bezier - start point \, one control point \, end point - next to the cubic 'curve' above., f 66;
#X msg 451 478 clear \, color 60 130 210 \, linewidth 6 \, arc 20 20 160 160 0 270 \, bang, f 44;
#X msg 451 508 clear \, color 200 80 60 \, arc 20 20 160 160 0 120 fill \, color 60 160 90 \, arc 20 20 160 160 120 360 fill \, bang, f 44;
#X msg 451 548 clear \, color 20 20 20 \, linewidth 3 \, quad 20 180 100 20 180 180 \, bang, f 44;
