#N canvas 169 133 1438 875 layers 0;
#X text 30 20 Each layer keeps its own drawing list and can be redrawn on its own \, which is much cheaper than redrawing everything. The 'layer' message picks the layer that the following commands are added to \, and the following 'bang' renders just that layer., f 64;
#X text 30 90 Layer 0 is the base layer \, drawn straight over the background. Extra layers are numbered from 1 upwards and are drawn on top of it. Use them in order: skipping one makes the object redraw everything instead., f 64;
#X text 30 144 Here the grid sits on layer 0 and only the moving dot on layer 1 is redrawn., f 64;
#X obj 340 330 else/guicanvas 200 120;
